{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `log_radon`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual likelihood accumulation inside the loop (`target += normal_lpdf(log_radon[n] | mu[n], sigma_y)`) with a vectorized built-in sampling statement, `log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y)`. The linear predictor `mu` is still computed deterministically from the same parameters and context data before the likelihood statement. No data values were changed or added.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> J;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county_idx;
  vector[N] floor_measure;
  vector[N] log_radon;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] alpha;
  real beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
}
model {
  vector[N] mu;
  // Prior
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta ~ normal(0, 10);

  // Linear predictor
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    mu[n] = alpha[county_idx[n]] + beta * floor_measure[n];
  }

  // Likelihood
  log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":2,"N":2,"county_idx":[2,2],"floor_measure":[6.625471726641565,2.9305997597925764],"log_radon":[5.9236580135561265,4.804899488499247]}","protected_variables":["log_radon"]}
